Linux: build only the Wayland backend and omit WebRTC and screen capture.
Reuse the existing no-media backend, reject room creation/joining, and remove
live collaboration controls, key bindings, and microphone recording. Keep local editing and Git.
Use the packaged cargo-about with its --fail check for license generation.

Omit obsolete WebRTC library search paths and honor release commit metadata.

